+---
+id: dl-005-createpatch-recursive-minimal-diff-using-add-remove-replace-arrays-trimmed-at-both-ends
+type: decision-log
+title: "createPatch: recursive minimal diff using add/remove/replace, arrays trimmed at both ends"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+
+## Context
+Clients need a patch describing only what changed between two versions, not the whole document.
+
+## Decision
+- Recursive diff: objects member by member, arrays by position; type mismatches and scalar changes become `replace` (root change: `replace` at `""`).
+- Only `add`, `remove` and `replace` are emitted; `move`/`copy`/`test` are not (simple, deterministic output).
+- Arrays: trim common prefix and suffix first, so a single insertion or removal yields one operation; the middle is diffed by position, extras removed last-first or appended.
+- Equality ignores member order (as `test`); output order follows key insertion order, so it is deterministic.
+- Values are deep-cloned into the patch.
+
+## Consequences
+- Output is small for typical edits but not guaranteed to be the shortest possible patch (no LCS, no move detection).
+- Round trip with `applyPatch` holds for all JSON inputs.
